{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1553122571,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MjM1MDg0MDg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3253","origin":"github"},"title":"--explicit prevents run from committing sidecar files","message":"When `run` is called with an `--output` that is more specific than just `.`, using `--sidecar` as well as `--explicit` will result in an untracked sidecar file.\nSince the sidecar file is determined by `run` itself, it doesn't make sense to me, to expect the user to specify it as an output (only a rather unspecific `.datalad/runinfo` would be possible to specify, which is running against the intention of `--explicit`).\n\nI have a quick fix already, but will come up with a proper test and possibly a nicer solution. Filing just the issue for now, in case somebody else runs into it. Just too late tonight to finish it. ;-)","files":null}]}